# MQ15 "Paradise". MQ14 100 set MQ15 10. Martin opens the portal (15); the player arrives in Camoran's Paradise
# (20). The dremora Kathutet guards the way out of the Savage Garden; the player chooses battle (32) and takes the
# Bands of the Chosen from him (45), which open the Forbidden Grotto (50). There Eldamil offers help (54, 56): the
# player plays the prisoner in his cage (57 .. 67), goes on (68) and has the Bands removed (70, 72). At Carac
# Agaialor Camoran's children greet the player (75), Mankar speaks (78 .. 80) and dies (89); Paradise dissolves and
# the player is back at Cloud Ruler Temple with the Amulet (90 .. 92). Martin puts it on (95) and names the last
# step, Chancellor Ocato (100).
# DRAFT from tools/live/quest_brief.py (2026-11-13): not run yet.

# Martin's greeting at 10 ("I have everything in place for the ritual ...", INFO 00027E38) offers "Yes, open the
# portal to Paradise." (INFO 00027E44, 15); his package MQ15MartinOpenPortal runs the ritual, which enables the door MQRitualMainRef (MQ15PortalRef is only a marker). Stepping through
# puts the player in the cell Paradise, where MQ15Script sets 20.
case mq15_portal
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 10
# Martin walks back to Cloud Ruler Temple; his portal greeting (and its choice) is given only in the Great Hall.
# The journal at 10 sends the player there ("meet Martin in the Great Hall"), so the player waits in the hall.
run
coc CloudRulerTempleGreatHall
until 7200 MartinRef.GetInCell CloudRulerTempleGreatHall == 1
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
approach MartinRef
talk MartinRef
ask "Yes, open the portal to Paradise."
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 15
bye if open
until 3600 MQRitualDrawingRef.stage == 2
run
player.moveto MQRitualMainRef
wait 120
activate MQRitualMainRef
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 20
end

# Kathutet (KathutetRef): his greeting ("You destroyed the Sigil Tower at Ganonah ...", INFO 0003C93C) offers "I
# seek Mankar Camoran." -> "What do you want, then?" (INFO 0003E8F4, MQ15 < 30) -> "I choose battle." (INFO
# 0003E8F7, 32). The player kills him and takes the Bands from his body (MQ15BracersScript OnAdd: 45); kill and
# RemoveAllItems stand in for the fight and the looting. The grotto's own daedra can attack him mid-conversation
# (run 58c): the player fights them, as a player would. `defend` covers only an attacker OF him; the cave daedra
# MQ15CavesDaedra100 (000998EF) is one HE attacks, which cut his conversation again in 60a (18th), so the player
# deals with it before talking.
case mq15_kathutet
defend KathutetRef
run
player.moveto KathutetRef
wait 120
run
000998EF.kill
approach KathutetRef
talk KathutetRef
ask "I seek Mankar Camoran."
ask "What do you want, then?"
ask "I choose battle."
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 32
bye if open
run
KathutetRef.kill
wait 60
run
KathutetRef.RemoveAllItems player
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 45
expect player.GetItemCount MQ15Bracers >= 1
end

# The Forbidden Grotto: the outer door (MQ15GrottoDoorEnter) is plain. The inner door MQ15CAMGrotto1ToGrotto2
# (MQ15GrottoEntranceScript) opens only to a wearer of the Bands, after its message box "The bands emit a red glow
# and the door opens." [Done]. MQ15Script sets 50 once the player is in ParadiseGrotto02.
case mq15_grotto
defend
run
player.equipitem MQ15Bracers
player.moveto MQ15GrottoDoorEnter
wait 120
activate MQ15GrottoDoorEnter
until 600 player.GetInCell ParadiseGrotto01 == 1
run
player.moveto MQ15CAMGrotto1ToGrotto2
wait 120
activate MQ15CAMGrotto1ToGrotto2
button 0
until 600 GetStage MQ15 >= 50
end

# Eldamil (EldamilRef): his greeting ("You wear the Bands, but you're no prisoner ...", INFO 00015746) sets 54 and
# offers "I'm here to kill Mankar Camoran." -> "Why would you help me?" -> "How can you help me?" (INFO 0003FBE2)
# -> "Fine. I'll play along." (INFO 0003FBE3, 56).
case mq15_eldamil
run
player.moveto EldamilRef
wait 120
approach EldamilRef
talk EldamilRef
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 54
ask "I'm here to kill Mankar Camoran."
ask "Why would you help me?"
ask "How can you help me?"
ask "Fine. I'll play along."
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 56
bye if open
end

# The cage: the dremora Orthe questions Eldamil (57; "Of course, kynreeve." sets 58); the player steps into the
# cage (within 50 of MQ15PlayerCageMarker: 60), Eldamil works the lever (EldamilScript OnPackageDone
# MQ15EldamilActivateCage: 62), the cage goes down (65) and comes up (66), and Eldamil's last warning sets 67.
case mq15_cage
until 3600 GetStage MQ15 >= 58
run
player.moveto MQ15PlayerCageMarker
until 600 GetStage MQ15 >= 60
until 3600 GetStage MQ15 >= 62
# 64 is the alarm (OrtheScript: hit, or the player not in the cage). Past 66 the player is an enemy again and Orthe's
# OnStartCombat sets it by design, so it is checked here, before the cage comes back up.
expect GetStageDone MQ15 64 == 0
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 65
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 66
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 67
end

# ParadiseGrotto03 (door MQ15CAMGrotto2ToGrotto3) sets 68. Eldamil's greeting there ("You made it ...", INFO
# 00047226) sets 70 and takes the Bands; "Sure. I'd be glad of your help." (INFO 000473C7) sets 72.
case mq15_bands_off
defend
run
player.moveto MQ15CAMGrotto2ToGrotto3
wait 120
activate MQ15CAMGrotto2ToGrotto3
button 0
until 600 GetStage MQ15 >= 68
until 3600 EldamilRef.GetDistance player < 1500
approach EldamilRef
talk EldamilRef
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 70
until 300 player.GetItemCount MQ15Bracers == 0
ask "Sure. I'd be glad of your help."
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 72
bye if open
end

# Carac Agaialor: Ruma and Raven Camoran greet the player (75); within 525 of Mankar the script sets 78, his speech
# ends at 79 ("Let us see who at last has proved the stronger!") and the script sets 80. kill stands in for the
# fight: MankarCamoranScript OnDeath sets 89 and, 15 s later, moves the player to MQ15PortalRef at Cloud Ruler
# Temple, where MQ15Script sets 90, 91 and 92 and the player holds the Amulet of Kings.
case mq15_mankar
defend
# Mankar waits at his throne (REFR 00084A2E, the location of MankarCamoranSitInThrone). A move to Mankar himself
# while his cell was not loaded left the player 1,227 from him (run 59d), so the player goes to the throne, as a
# player walks up to it. The throne is not persistent, so the move to Mankar loads its cell first.
run
player.moveto MankarCamoranRef
wait 60
run
player.moveto 00084A2E
wait 120
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 78
until 3600 GetStage MQ15 >= 80
run
MankarCamoranRef.kill
until 600 GetStage MQ15 >= 89
until 3600 GetStage MQ15 >= 90
until 1800 GetStage MQ15 >= 92
expect player.GetItemCount AmuletofKings >= 1
# At 92 Martin comes to the player (MQ15MartinGreetPlayer, a force-greet), so no case boundary here: the game cannot
# save with his conversation open. His greeting ("You found a way back! Does this mean... ?", INFO 0003782B) offers
# "Mankar Camoran is dead." -> "Here. The Amulet belongs to you." -> "Put on the Amulet, your Majesty." (INFO
# 00037830, 95) -> "You see, you are Uriel's son." -> "You are the Emperor." -> "Why meet Ocato?" (INFO 0004BF99, 100).
hear 1800 MartinRef You found a way back
wait 30
talk MartinRef
ask "Mankar Camoran is dead."
ask "Here. The Amulet belongs to you."
ask "Put on the Amulet, your Majesty."
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 95
expect player.GetItemCount AmuletofKings == 0
ask "You see, you are Uriel's son."
ask "You are the Emperor."
ask "Why meet Ocato?"
until 300 GetStageDone MQ15 100
bye if open
end
